{"kind": "mod", "id": 1621, "name": "Shadow Flicker Fix", "slug": "shadow-flicker-fix", "teaser": "Fixes distant shadow flickering which was most noticeable with anti-aliasing disabled.", "owner_name": "pein", "downloads": 68958, "favourites": 84, "featured": false, "contains_ads": false, "contains_ai_content": false, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": "MIT License", "guid": "com.pein.shadowflickerfix", "thumbnail_local": null, "category": null, "category_id": null, "updated_at": "2026-07-28T06:13:51.000000Z", "created_at": "2024-08-04T16:18:40.000000Z", "published_at": "2024-08-04T16:18:40.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~4.0.0", "latest_version": "1.5.2", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": "https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/", "description_html": "<h3>Introduction</h3>\n<p>This mod fixes distant shadow flickering which was most noticeable with anti-aliasing disabled. Also includes options to configure some shadow-related variables, enable SMAA and configure TAA.</p>\n<h3>Performance</h3>\n<p>In testing I saw a very minimal performance impact, if at all. However, if you feel like your game is running worse then consider changing the Distant Shadow Resolution option in the config. Enabling shadow changes will most likely reduce FPS by some amount depending on the config.</p>\n<h3>Preview</h3>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.imgur.com/qkVjdtZ.gif\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/qkVjdtZ.gif\" alt=\"qkVjdtZ.gif\" /></a></p>\n<h3>Installation</h3>\n<p>Just drag and drop the BepInEx folder into your SPT folder.</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.imgur.com/wByb5Ln.gif\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/wByb5Ln.gif\" alt=\"wByb5Ln.gif\" /></a></p>\n", "versions": [{"version": "1.3.0", "spt_version_constraint": "~3.10.0", "content_length": null, "dow